{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium","id":1492459,"title":"Beast Homebrew Compendium","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-06T15:47:15-07:00","id":1492459,"title":"Beast Homebrew Compendium","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1cEcqWx5t5qhrCTKZTVD69kuX0ONn953z2zdoWva5U2U/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Click here.</b></a> Of note is that this document includes homebrew written by myself and others, and I have edited many of them to better suit my purposes if I ever ST Beast. If you do not see your homebrew included here, I either didn't see it, or just didn't think it's something I wanna include in my hypothetical Beast Chronicle, nothing personal. Big thanks to everyone whose homebrew made it into this document, y'all are cool people. I'll be adding a lot of Nightmares to this document soon, as well. If anybody has new ideas for Beast homebrew, do post them here so we can discuss them and I can add them to the document for everybody's ease of perusal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T09:27:34-07:00","id":1492984,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That is really helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T15:38:34-07:00","id":1496133,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> I have included your <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\"><b>Beast Homebrew Hub</b></a> in the hyperlink for the compendium in the original post. Wonderful creations all around, you should be proud of yourself! Do you think you could read through the compendium and give some feedback, please?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> I also included your <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1033582-fear-club\"><b>Fear Club</b></a>, since it's cool too, and your input is likewise welcome.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Have you homebrewed anything you'd like me to include and discuss, since you are also a very important figure in the Beast fandom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T16:29:31-07:00","id":1496137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1496133#post1496133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> Have you homebrewed anything you'd like me to include and discuss, since you are also a very important figure in the Beast fandom?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like in a complete form? Probably not, both on the forums and in my notes. A lot of my homebrew is stuff I either just implement in games and know it off hand, or is stuff I'm playtesting in said games before trying to pin it down. <br /> <br /> EDIT: to iterate, a lot of the stuff I have is not, like, homebrew in the traditional sense. A lot of my stuff is 2E/ Supplement dev stuff, not just me making my game work a certain way to my liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-02-2022, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T17:03:48-07:00","id":1496138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1496137#post1496137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like in a complete form? Probably not, both on the forums and in my notes. A lot of my homebrew is stuff I either just implement in games and know it off hand, or is stuff I'm playtesting in said games before trying to pin it down.<br /> <br /> EDIT: to iterate, a lot of the stuff I have is not, like, homebrew in the traditional sense. A lot of my stuff is 2E/ Supplement dev stuff, not just me making my game work a certain way to my liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood. What about all those long-form essays and such? I think one of them had the words &quot;teeth &amp; gin&quot; in the title, and I also recall various threads about apparent crossovers, with names like &quot;the Anakim &amp; The Invincible&quot; or thereabouts. Do you think you could compile a list of the thread titles for all such essays and essay-adjacent writings related to Beast, and post that list here, please? I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has written several threads like that, though he usually calls them some variant of &quot;musings&quot;. Speak up if you're reading this, Satchel. I'd be happy if you also gave me a list of your musing-threads about Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T17:36:20-07:00","id":1496141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1496138#post1496138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understood. What about all those long-form essays and such? I think one of them had the words &quot;teeth &amp; gin&quot; in the title, and I also recall various threads about apparent crossovers, with names like &quot;the Anakim &amp; The Invincible&quot; or thereabouts. Do you think you could compile a list of the thread titles for all such essays and essay-adjacent writings related to Beast, and post that list here, please? I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> has written several threads like that, though he usually calls them some variant of &quot;musings&quot;. Speak up if you're reading this, Satchel. I'd be happy if you also gave me a list of your musing-threads about Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1402882-whiskey-gin-and-teeth-arcane-wrote-some-things\">Whiskey, Gin, and Teeth</a> is, in fact, Arc's compilation thread with the links to all her essays, including the threads looking at subtypes of Hero as responses to the fears the Families represent.<br /> <br /> I haven't got a list of those threads for my own stuff at the moment, because most of my Beast thoughts that aren't in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1422382-legend-embellishment-and-the-siege-of-the-bright-dream-assorted-brainstorming\">the brainstorming thread</a> I put up and have been using as a place to examine the game's concepts in general are instead just out loose in the wild in other threads as individual posts. I'll see what I can pull together when I get the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T18:22:13-08:00","id":1497248,"title":"","content":"This is fantastic, thank you for compiling this! Long time admirer of your homebrew!<br /> <br /> I have these rules that I have used in my Beast games, what do y'all think?<br /> <br /> <b>Primordial Pathway Chamber Reflection</b><br /> <br /> Opening a Primordial Pathway in the place the Chamber is reflected in no longer requires a roll, and can enter the Lair without a willpower cost (for either the Beast or the Cultists). It remains for a scene, but can be closed early by the opener.<br /> <br /> <b>Merging and Horrors</b><br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to merge with your Horror when you enter your Lair or open a Primordial Pathway, unless there is immediate danger or an intruder. <br /> <br /> When merged with your horror, you can use any aspect of an Atavism - normal, low Satiety, or Satiety expenditure, though the latter still requires spending Satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":27667,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","user":"Super Vlad","date":".  Added my own homebrew rule! 11-15-2022, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T23:08:40-08:00","id":1497265,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I read your threads for the Forswearing that corresponds to each Family. Good job! Any plans for the ones which correspond to the Inguma and Talasii?<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think Hunger-equivalents for Heroes would be like? Could they be similar to my old idea of Yearnings from my not-so-good attempt at modelling Princesses as pseudo-Beasts? I like the idea that a Forswearing is a rejection of fear, while a Yearning guides a Hero on what must replace fear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hunger for Prey becomes the Yearning for Friendship, and Predators become Companions. They nurture lasting bonds and restore broken ones by revealing the humanity that exists inside of and in tandem with monstrosity.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Power becomes the Yearning for Freedom, and Tyrants become Liberators. They stand up for those who cannot defend themselves and give opportunities for others to fulfill their true potential.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Hoard becomes the Yearning for Prosperity, and Collectors become Benefactors. They cater to the physical and emotional needs of others, and help them become independent enough to thrive on their own merits.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Ruin becomes the Yearning for Safety, and Ravagers become Sentinels. They renew other people's belief in order, law or equivalent ideal by providing support networks for those who have suffered terrible losses.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Punishment becomes the Yearning for Forgiveness, and Nemeses become Diplomats. They convince others to overcome grievances and understand wrongdoings by finding methods of compromise that acknowledge each side of a conflict.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Secrets becomes the Yearning for Trust, and Whisperers become Confidants. They protect secrets that would cause more bad than good if they ever got out, and help others deal with the consequences if they do decide to reveal the secrets.<br /> <br /> The Hunger for Transgression becomes the Yearning for Wisdom, and Enablers become Advisers. They let others know when there are better options and guide them toward sensible answers. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T23:26:35-08:00","id":1497266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497265#post1497265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I read your threads for the Forswearing that corresponds to each Family. Good job! Any plans for the ones which correspond to the Inguma and Talasii?<br /> <br /> Also, what do you think Hunger-equivalents for Heroes would be like? Could they be similar to my old idea of Yearnings from my not-so-good attempt at modelling Princesses as pseudo-Beasts? I like the idea that a Forswearing is a rejection of fear, while a Yearning guides a Hero on what must replace fear.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've gone on record saying that the Hunger equivalent for Heroes is Hunger. Hunger is the universal of Primordial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T23:35:01-08:00","id":1497267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497266#post1497266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gone on record saying that the Hunger equivalent for Heroes is Hunger. Hunger is the universal of Primordial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, though? Aren't Heroes supposed to be metaphysically closer to the Bright Dream, at least in theory? I don't get it. Can they even store Satiety like Beasts can? If they can't do that, why give them Hungers? IDK, it just feels weird to me, and maybe it would result in Heroes who have too much personality-overlap with Beasts? Not even in the IC sense of <u><i>&quot;we're not so different, you and I...&quot;</i></u>. I mean more of an OOC impression of sameness and predictability. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T07:34:44-08:00","id":1497283,"title":"","content":"I added a magical item system in the homebrew compendium called &quot;Nightmarish Crafting&quot;, inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27667_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27667\" data-vbnamecard=\"27667\">Super Vlad</a>'s Primordial Shards, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>'s Enmantled Tokens and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1130_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1130\" data-vbnamecard=\"1130\">falco1029</a>'s Sanguine Crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T09:43:38-08:00","id":1497286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497267#post1497267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, though? Aren't Heroes supposed to be metaphysically closer to the Bright Dream, at least in theory? I don't get it. Can they even store Satiety like Beasts can? If they can't do that, why give them Hungers? IDK, it just feels weird to me, and maybe it would result in Heroes who have too much personality-overlap with Beasts? Not even in the IC sense of <u><i>&quot;we're not so different, you and I...&quot;</i></u>. I mean more of an OOC impression of sameness and predictability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes use the Bright Dream to deny the Primordial Dream, at first in mircocosm and then spreading outwards from there-but you can only lie to yourself so much.<br /> <br /> The Bright Dream and Primordial Dreams aren't in opposition to each other-the Bright Dream sprang from the Primordial Dream dreaming things up in pursuit of Satiety. Human advancement is a long line of humans finding cleverer and cleverer ways to not only eat, but to Sate their own Hunger. At the most extreme, the Bright Dream has done this so well that it feels disconnected from the Primordial, which may be one of the reasons why the Dark Mother raised Beasts(/Insatiable, depending on how dark you wanna go)-but at the end of the day, they do have a harmony between them. So much of Primordial is about that fact.<br /> <br /> So this is the point. Heroes can deny the reason why they're Hungry, but they still gotta Eat. The Insatiable think reasons' the problem in the first place, and make excess of Hunger to destroy reason. Beasts understand the relationship between their Nightmares and their Hungers, and seek to make more of themselves by making them transcendent. The overlap is there because the overlap is where the conversation is being had<br /> <br /> Hunger is the universal because everything bites, everything needs to feed. We all need some of the security that the Hungers represent, the safety and stress relief that comes with power, hoard, predation, punishment, ruin, privacy and knowledge, and transgression. Society is often at it's best when it acknowledges those needs, and it's worst when it overindulges. It is the thing that Primordial as a game cannot ignore, that it has to address.<br /> <br /> If you asked me to reduce the game down to one of it's elements to make it's point, it's Hunger. Nothing else comes even close to being the tip of the spear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T22:30:53-08:00","id":1497342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497286#post1497286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heroes use the Bright Dream to deny the Primordial Dream, at first in mircocosm and then spreading outwards from there-but you can only lie to yourself so much.<br /> <br /> The Bright Dream and Primordial Dreams aren't in opposition to each other-the Bright Dream sprang from the Primordial Dream dreaming things up in pursuit of Satiety. Human advancement is a long line of humans finding cleverer and cleverer ways to not only eat, but to Sate their own Hunger. At the most extreme, the Bright Dream has done this so well that it feels disconnected from the Primordial, which may be one of the reasons why the Dark Mother raised Beasts(/Insatiable, depending on how dark you wanna go)-but at the end of the day, they do have a harmony between them. So much of Primordial is about that fact.<br /> <br /> So this is the point. Heroes can deny the reason why they're Hungry, but they still gotta Eat. The Insatiable think reasons' the problem in the first place, and make excess of Hunger to destroy reason. Beasts understand the relationship between their Nightmares and their Hungers, and seek to make more of themselves by making them transcendent. The overlap is there because the overlap is where the conversation is being had<br /> <br /> Hunger is the universal because everything bites, everything needs to feed. We all need some of the security that the Hungers represent, the safety and stress relief that comes with power, hoard, predation, punishment, ruin, privacy and knowledge, and transgression. Society is often at it's best when it acknowledges those needs, and it's worst when it overindulges. It is the thing that Primordial as a game cannot ignore, that it has to address.<br /> <br /> If you asked me to reduce the game down to one of it's elements to make it's point, it's Hunger. Nothing else comes even close to being the tip of the spear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I'll make my Playable Heroes have Hungers, then. But I'll add Yearnings as an optional mechanic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T14:26:58-08:00","id":1497418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497342#post1497342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I'll make my Playable Heroes have Hungers, then. But I'll add Yearnings as an optional mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting what the Positive Opposite of Hunger design will do for a game of Beast.<br /> <br /> Namely, it guarentees Heroes will always be in the moral right.<br /> <br /> Heroes, even without what I want to do with them for the Storyteller's Guide/2E, are supposed to be antagonists with dubious moral position against Beasts-maybe not universally actually bad, or least, any worse than Beasts, maybe sometimes even well justified, but it's always enough of a question to make you wonder whether the &quot;institutional&quot; bias of Beasts is warranted. Usually, it is, because there is a willingness to commit similar monstrosity while placing themselves above Beasts, but there's enough room for Beasts to be really bad and for some Heroes to be trying to do good that Beasts have to wrestle against that bias and be willing to contend with Heroes as individuals, having the conflict that Heroes seemingly never have. They are both assholes who start at the dark gray line between the usual gray morality of Chronicles protagonists and the black of their antagonists, and have the latitude to move up and down from there.<br /> <br /> So, if Heroes just absolutely hunger for wholly positive pursuit, that ruins all of that. No Beast, no matter how good they may want to be, is going to compete with an entity whose metaphysical health is dependent on being, at a minimum, more moral than someone who doesn't have that account. There may be something to explore in the idea of a person who feels compelled and existentially dependent on doing constructive acts and how much one can count that as moral choice, and of course it's relationship to harm done in the name of morality, but that's fairly narrow.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason why, in my own work on this, I gave them both Hunger, is that it anchors this element of similar kind of assholery where one is not actually better than the other. By making them oppose Fear ala contrasting the Families creates a reason they can be an attractive form of transgression over the other-who doesn't want to root for someone who gathers power and hoard and secrets, who pursues punishment or facilitates transgression, who wrecks predation and ruin upon other in the name of Victory, Enlightenment, Humility and Hearth, Health and Wholeness, Safety, Unity, and Liberation-but we can keep it clear that it's all the same sort of shit by making the ends and the means the same.<br /> <br /> Another advantage towards the approach is that it allows us to talk about Hunger <i>as</i> constructive-Yes, a Beast causes shock and loss with feeding, but after that, with some limits due ot tangibility, a Hungry Child can then possibly give the taken thing <i>back</i>, or to the worthy, or to people who need it. They have room to completely destroy it if it's too much of a thing of strife, or to keep it and work to transform it into something that is better for the community. They can, of course, also do none of those things.<br /> <br /> And finally, it does deny talking about the systemic problems that contribute to <i>why</i> Heroes get more press than Beasts, the way that the Monomyth shares space with Mummy's Law of Suffering and Mage's Lie and the presence of the God-Machine and the threat of the True Fae, and more asides.<br /> <br /> Also, like, you want a game about the horror of those dedicated to moral ends, Mummy: The Curse (aka, The Better Angel Game) is next door.<br /> <br /> food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-17-2022, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T19:14:34-08:00","id":1497441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497267#post1497267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why, though? Aren't Heroes supposed to be metaphysically closer to the Bright Dream, at least in theory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna chime in on this from a couple turns back in the conversation:<br /> <br /> The Bright Dream is not a morally better place than the Dark Dream. Everything in the Astral is id, to one degree or another; just because Temenotic Goetia aren't the personal fixations of an individual mind or the Dreamtime's participants in the great game of adaptation doesn't mean that they have any especial business pretending they aren't the literal representatives of culture war \u2014 it's the collective unconscious, nobody is holding them to a moral standard.<br /> <br /> Yes, a recurring motif in the Chronicles is that the magical power associated with sociable humanity tends to be the ability to Say No To The Supernatural, but that doesn't make the driving impetus behind that denial the reverse of the crocodile-brain Hungers tap into. The superego as a character is not morally superior to the id as a character just because the one opposes the other \u2014 the fact that I keep coming back to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1398660-some-assembly-required-houserules-and-beast-the-primordial?p=1401844#post1401844\">&quot;thank god she's on our side&quot;</a> as a recurring tint to Beasts as morally commendable actors should tell you something when the defining features of Heroes that Beasts tend to be concerned with in the modern era is &quot;opposes Beasts,&quot; not &quot;does good where Beasts do bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Bright Dream is Bright because it's got other people in it, but the conceptual forces behind the human psyche have the same fundamentals as the ones behind the soul of the world. Entropy takes her due \u2014 it's inner demons all the way down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T19:32:17-08:00","id":1497443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1492459-beast-homebrew-compendium?p=1497441#post1497441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The superego as a character is not morally superior to the id as a character just because the one opposes the other \u2014</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/zZNKOxBqMh8?t=298\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;It sounds like you're just rationalizing every evil decision you make just to convince yourself it's right.&quot;<br /> &quot;Uh, yeah-superego, that's pretty much what I do.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> Finally a good excuse to link to Sam &amp; Max: The Devil's Playhouse.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Heroes are to persona and superego what Beasts(and Insatiable's more so) are to shadow and id.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-18-2022, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-20T10:10:23-08:00","id":1497636,"title":"","content":"Added some new features for my Playable Hero Template based on the recent observations of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> in this thread and elsewhere, mainly Hungers, Forswearing and a new Heroic Gift called Manifest Archetype.<br /> <br /> Added part of the homebrewed Nightmares from the Beast forums, and will add the rest soon.<br /> <br /> Added rules for Beastly Magic Items called Viscera, akin to Tokens in Changeling 2ed, plus a Magic Item Craftsman Merit for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Added an equivalent of Lair Resonance for Nightmares rather than Atavisms, which I've named &quot;Your Worst Nightmare&quot;.<br /> <br /> Buffed the Macabre Insight Merit so it interfaces with Your Worst Nightmare.<br /> <br /> Added Satchel's musings-thread for Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-20-2022, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T14:31:45-07:00","id":1506262,"title":"","content":"Added sketches of new supernatural abilities to my Playable Hero Template based on the writings of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. I have no clue if it's any good, or all that similar to their respective initial visions, but I'm open to critiques on how to improve my execution.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><u><b>Journeying:</b></u><br /> <br /> Rather than having Lairs, Heroes can call forth the Bright Dream to manifest storytelling tropes in baseline reality and enforce the validity of their worldviews and identities as they pertain to the Monomyth. These are called Journey Traits, and Heroes start with 3 of them: 1 based on Forswearing, 1 based on Legend, and 1 based on Hunger. They are classified into Minor and Major, and at least 1 must be Minor.<br /> <br /> Each 1 dot of Destiny after the 1st allows the player to pick +1 Journey Trait, which must be linked to the Forswearing, Legend or Hunger, with each of these able to receive up to 3 Journey Traits. Journeying requires 1 Willpower Point and a roll of [Attribute + Skill], with the bonuses and penalties being based on the feasibility of the story-logic that the Hero is attempting to actively manifest. If the player lets the ST choose the details of how the Journey Trait manifests, the cost of 1 Willpower Point is waived.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Roll Results [Journeying]:</b></u><br /> <br /> \u2022 Dramatic Failure: The Journeying goes terribly wrong and the corpse of the Horror that the Hero partially slayed during his Conquering returns to life for the scene. Said Horror has a Rank equal to the Hero\u2019s Destiny and can open Primordial Pathways into baseline reality, but automatically returns to the Hero\u2019s mind and becomes comatose again at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> The Horror will do everything it can to make the Hero succumb to the type of fear that was rejected during the Hero\u2019s Conquering, and thus potentially cause the beginning of a Devouring to transform the Hero into a Beast of the Family that corresponds to his Forswearing, though the Hero\u2019s Hunger might change due to the drastic shift.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Failure: The Journeying fails to manifest but the roll can be retried with a cumulative -1 penalty. Repeated attempts increase the chances of nearby Beasts noticing the presence of the Hero via Family Resemblance or equivalent supernatural ability. Spent Willpower Points are not regained.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Success: The Journeying manifests, and has a pool of points equal to [Successes] + [Destiny], which can impose bonuses and penalties for specific types of rolls on a 1 to 1 ratio. Besides dice modifiers, the Hero can also introduce narrative declarations modeled as free-form Conditions, and each such Condition can be worth 1, 2 or 3 Journeying points, depending on its usefulness for the Hero. The effects must be mundane and last for the scene, or until the Hero dismisses them as a reflexive action. Increase the cost of Journeying points by +2 if the Condition is Persistent, which allows its effects to last beyond this scene. However, a Beast can potentially circumvent or undo such effects with his Atavisms, Nightmares and Lairs Traits, and the same goes for the supernatural powers of other monsters.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Exceptional Success: As per Success, but the Hero can also introduce narrative declarations and/or dice modifiers whose effects are supernatural or otherwise extreme, due to the Bright Dream significantly bridging the gap between reality and the imaginary. The Hero imposes a Clash Of Wills consisting of [Highest Resistance Attribute + Destiny] against supernatural attempts to circumvent or undo the effects of his Journeying. The Hero gains a dice trick if he has placed an thematically fitting Anathema on a Beast, based on the latter\u2019s Satiety Level as defined by Anathemas: Low Satiety = 9 Again, Middle Satiety = 8 Again, High Satiety = Rote Quality. This extends to Kin who have Family Ties to the Beast suffering from the Anathema.<br /> \u200b<br /> <u><b>Example Of Journeying:</b></u><br /> <br /> Consider a Hero who has the Forswearing of Invincible, Legend of Judgmental, and Hunger of Whisperer. His initial Journey Traits could work like this:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Forswearing [Major]: Nobody suffers the fear of Exposure embodied by the Ugallu, even if it would be rational to do so. Those affected would walk naked into the street and glibly share all their secrets, which can be modeled as the Spooked Condition, but re-skinned as a Careless Condition that compels them to lower their suspicions and inhibitions around anyone who seems even minimally trustworthy.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Legend [Minor]: Individuals that weaponize the fear of judgment get marked in some way, such as a mortal journalist getting their car vandalized, or an Ugallu Tyrant finding himself caught in the middle of an angry mob of protesters. This can be modeled as bonus dice for relevant rolls (e.g. Wits + Investigation to decipher the message carved onto the mortal journalist\u2019s car, Manipulation + Subterfuge to provoke rage in the Ugallu Tyrant via accusations disguised as questions).<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hunger [Minor or Major]: Those who are predisposed to revealing others\u2019 secrets are compelled to do so and are presented with viable opportunities, thus outing them as monsters. This in turn attracts people who are scared of having their secrets revealed (e.g. people with the Embarrassing Secret Condition), which can contribute to them potentially becoming Hunters, Heroes or even Beasts.<br /> <br /> This can be modeled similarly to the &quot;We Know All You Secrets&quot; Nightmare, with Normal Satiety if the Journey Trait is Minor, or with High Satiety if the Journey Trait is Major, and scoring the same number of Successes as the Journeying. If the player waived the cost of 1 Willpower Point to let the ST decide the details of the Journeying, but spends 1 Willpower Point regardless, then the effective activation of the \u201cWe Know All Your Secrets\u201d Nightmare is considered to benefit from Satiety Expenditure.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this Journey Trait imposes a pseudo-Lair Trait based on the Hunger for Secrets. Perhaps the Minor version of the Journey Trait makes it harder to communicate sensitive information without being overheard (i.e. Echoing), while the Major version of the Journey Trait unlocks doors and windows that lead to places full of incriminating evidence (i.e. Exposed). \u200bIf the player waived the cost of 1 Willpower Point to let the ST decide the details of the Journeying, but spends 1 Willpower Point regardless, then this pseudo-Lair Trait can introduce narrative declarations in the form of Persistent Conditions without the additional cost of 2 Journeying points.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Additional examples of Journeying:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A Hero who has the Forswearing of Victorious, Legend of Competitive and Hunger for Power could be a boxing champion who got bored of fighting humans and decided to revitalize his dwindling career by fighting monsters. He could have a Major Journey Trait linked to his Legend with the name of &quot;I Always Find A Weapon Lying Around&quot;, such as a bottle of wine on a shelf that he can break to use as an improvised shiv-like weapon, or a rusty lead pipe poking out of a dumpster he can pull out and use as an improvised club-like weapon. This is modeled similarly to the Razored Major Lair Trait of Beasts. Alternatively, it could be modeled similarly to the You Must Obey Nightmare, which compels nearby mortals to hand him objects he can use as weapons, akin to handing a folding metal chair to a wrestling champion.<br /> <br /> A Hero who has the Forswearing of Immortal, Legend of Vicious and Hunger for Ruin could be a domestic terrorist who was judged and persecuted long after he stopped working as a drug dealer, and decided to use chemical weapons to destroy things that represent the ignored ugliness of society in his worldview. He could have a Major Journey Trait linked to his Hunger with the name of &quot;I Always Find Ingredients For Bombs&quot;, such as mixing hygiene and kitchen products to make chlorine gas, or mixing hospital garbage and garden fertilizer to make Molotov cocktails. This is mechanically modeled similarly to the Toxic Major Lair Trait of Beasts. Alternatively, it could be modeled as the Run Away Nightmare, which provokes a similar kind of abject panic and flight response when the Hero's enemies are exposed to his chemical bombs.</div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-23-2023, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T20:43:21-07:00","id":1507256,"title":"","content":"Added significant revisions to my system for magic items of Beasts, with inspiration taken from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1498231-the-power-of-man-s-red-flower-idle-thoughts-on-possible-beast-crafting\"><b>this thread</b></a>. These revisions are under the Cyclopean Workshop Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}